int iteration = 10;
int result = 5;

// Compound Assignment with Postfix Decrement
// 1. Uses iteration (10) in the multiplication: result = 5 * 10
// 2. Decrements iteration to 9
result *= iteration--;

// State check (Safety Confirmation):
// result == 50
// iteration == 9

// Rule: Postfix guarantees the original
// value is used in the expression *before*
// the variable is modified.
